uot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#d33636&quot;}],&quot;xAxe&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;None&quot;,&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#000000&quot;,&quot;used&quot;:false},&quot;layout&quot;:{&quot;margin&quot;:{&quot;l&quot;:35,&quot;r&quot;:25,&quot;b&quot;:80,&quot;t&quot;:35},&quot;font&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#333333&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:11,&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;},&quot;paper_bgcolor&quot;:&quot;#ffffff&quot;,&quot;plot_bgcolor&quot;:&quot;#f8f8f8&quot;,&quot;bordercolor&quot;:&quot;#cccccc&quot;,&quot;yaxis&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;linear&quot;,&quot;gridcolor&quot;:&quot;#e0e0e0&quot;,&quot;showgrid&quot;:true},&quot;xaxis&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;linear&quot;,&quot;gridcolor&quot;:&quot;#e0e0e0&quot;,&quot;showgrid&quot;:true},&quot;showlegend&quot;:true,&quot;grid&quot;:{&quot;rows&quot;:1,&quot;columns&quot;:1,&quot;pattern&quot;:&quot;independent&quot;,&quot;roworder&quot;:&quot;bottom to top&quot;}},&quot;options&quot;:{},&quot;sweep&quot;:{&quot;param&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;values&quot;:&quot;[]&quot;}}"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="420" height="230"><div name="plots" style="border-style: double; transform-origin: 0px 0px; transform: scale(0.6); box-sizing: border-box; border-width: 3px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; width: 700px; height: 383.333px;" ondblclick="showPlotInModel(this)"></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(470,20)" x="470" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="845" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="845" style="width: 560px; height: 845px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 1508.93px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Full-Wave Bridge Rectifier Fed by a Transformer&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source (V1):&lt;/strong&gt; 50 Hz sine wave, 20 V peak&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Winding resistance (Rp):&lt;/strong&gt; 10 &amp;Omega; in series with the primary. A transformer winding is a short circuit in DC, so a small series resistance is always needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformer (T1):&lt;/strong&gt; L1 = 100 mH, L2 = 25 mH, M = 49.5 mH (coupling factor k = 0.99)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge (D1, D2, D3, D4):&lt;/strong&gt; four diodes: D1 A&amp;rarr;Out, D2 B&amp;rarr;Out, D3 gnd&amp;rarr;A, D4 gnd&amp;rarr;B&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter (C1):&lt;/strong&gt; 100 &amp;micro;F&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Load (R1):&lt;/strong&gt; 1 k&amp;Omega;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;The Transformer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$n = \dfrac{N_2}{N_1} = \sqrt{\dfrac{L_2}{L_1}} = \sqrt{\dfrac{25}{100}} = \dfrac{1}{2}$ &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; $V_{2,peak} \approx n\,V_{1,peak} = 0.5 \times 20 = \mathbf{10\ V}$
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The secondary is floating: its terminals A and B are tied to the circuit only through the diodes, which is exactly what the equations of the model need.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;How the Bridge Works&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Positive half-cycle (A above B)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;D1 and D4 conduct, D2 and D3 are blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path: A &amp;rarr; D1 &amp;rarr; Out &amp;rarr; R1 and C1 &amp;rarr; gnd &amp;rarr; D4 &amp;rarr; B&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node A is pulled up to Out + 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node B is pulled down to gnd &amp;minus; 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col red&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Negative half-cycle (B above A)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;D2 and D3 conduct, D1 and D4 are blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path: B &amp;rarr; D2 &amp;rarr; Out &amp;rarr; R1 and C1 &amp;rarr; gnd &amp;rarr; D3 &amp;rarr; A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node B is pulled up to Out + 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node A is pulled down to gnd &amp;minus; 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In both half-cycles the current crosses the load in the &lt;strong&gt;same direction&lt;/strong&gt;, so the load sees the absolute value of the secondary voltage minus two diode drops:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$V_{Out} \approx |V_A - V_B| - 2\,V_D \approx 10 - 2 \times 0.76 \approx 8.5\ V$ (first peak)
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;The Filter Capacitor&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;C1 is charged at every peak (twice per period of the source) and supplies the load between the peaks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$\Delta V \approx \dfrac{I_{load}}{2\,f\,C_1} = \dfrac{7.5\ mA}{2 \times 50 \times 100\ \mu F} \approx \mathbf{0.75\ V}$
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simulation (steady state):&lt;/strong&gt; Out varies between about 7.2 V and 7.8 V, a ripple of about 0.6 V at 100 Hz (twice the source frequency)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The formula is an upper bound: the capacitor does not discharge during the whole interval between two peaks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The peak is lower than the first one (8.5 V) because the current taken by C1 at each peak drops voltage in Rp and in the winding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Reading the Plot&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;B&lt;/strong&gt; (secondary): they swing in opposite directions; each one is clamped between about &amp;minus;0.8 V and Out + 0.76 V by the bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Out&lt;/strong&gt;: the filtered DC output, with a small ripple at 100 Hz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Things to Try&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change C1 to 1 mF: the ripple becomes about ten times smaller&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change R1 to 200 &amp;Omega;: the load current grows and so does the ripple&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change L2 to 100 mH and M to 99 mH: the ratio becomes 1:1 and Out rises to about 17 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove C1: Out follows the rectified wave (pulsating DC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card green-border&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;&quot;&gt;The transformer lowers the 20 V peak to 10 V, the four-diode bridge makes both half-cycles drive the load in the same direction, and C1 smooths the result: about 7.5 V DC with a 0.6 V ripple at twice the line frequency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
